/** Retrofit batch AT -- upgrading old 2-case gpe-history problems to the 4-case standard (Sample +
 * boundary + tricky + stress). All solvers below were independently written and verified byte-for-
 * byte against each problem's real official Sample before being trusted to generate new tricky/
 * stress expected output.
 *
 * gpe-10608-minimal-coverage: classic greedy interval-cover of [0,M] (sort by left endpoint, repeatedly
 *   extend coverage via the reachable segment with the furthest right endpoint). Despite the problem
 *   statement claiming a blank line between test-case outputs, the real sample shows NO blank line.
 * gpe-10609-square-root: BigInt Newton's-method integer square root. Unlike the other problems in this
 *   batch, the real sample DOES show a blank line between outputs -- matched via join("\n\n").
 * gpe-10610-curling-up-the-cube: BFS over the net's connected squares, tracking a 6-label cube-face
 *   orientation (top/bottom/north/south/east/west) via roll transforms as each adjacent square is
 *   visited; a net is a valid cube net iff exactly 6 distinct faces get touched with no reuse conflict.
 *   Same blank-line-claim-vs-real-sample mismatch as gpe-10608 -- no blank line in the real format.
 * gpe-10615-divisibility: multi-dimensional digit-DP (values are hypercube "staircase" sums, i.e.
 *   multinomial coefficients; by Kummer's theorem a coefficient is divisible by prime P iff any base-P
 *   digit addition of the coordinates carries) counting non-multiples of P via a tightness-bitmask DP
 *   per digit position, combined with 2^N-corner inclusion-exclusion to turn the [0,R]-only count into
 *   an [L,R] range count. Verified against brute-force Pascal's-triangle-style recurrences for both the
 *   boundary and tricky cases, and against all 3 real sample datasets exactly.
 * gpe-10636-gopher-ii: classic bipartite matching (Kuhn's algorithm) between gophers and reachable
 *   holes (distance <= s*v, with a small epsilon tolerance for exact-boundary distances); the answer is
 *   the number of unmatched gophers.
 * gpe-10637-tight-words: DP over "current last digit" tracking counts of tight words of increasing
 *   length (each step only allows moving to an adjacent digit value), output as a percentage of all
 *   (k+1)^n possible words.
 * gpe-10642-marbles: EGF-based inclusion-exclusion DP over "boxes filled so far", using a prefix-scaled
 *   convolution per box to count distinguishable-marble distributions with each box >= X marbles,
 *   modulo 1e9+7. The stress case keeps N well under the stated 100000 upper bound since this direct
 *   convolution DP is O(K*N^2) (an FFT/NTT-based solution would be needed to reach O(K*N log N) at
 *   N=100000); N=8000 already takes real time to generate and stresses an O(K*N^2) reference solidly.
 */
